  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a twenty-four song set on Sunday, December 10, 2023, at the Thunderbird Music Hall in Pittsburgh, PA [1][5]. This concert is the 399th of 467 archived shows for the band, following a performance at the Center for the Arts on December 8, 2023 [4]. The recording, titled MountainGoats2023-12-10, is the only available capture of this event and runs for 111 minutes [1]. It was taped and transferred by Alex Herd [1]. The setlist includes tracks such as “Jenny III,” “Murder at the 18th St. Garage,” and “Dark in Here” [1]. Notable moments include “Design Your Own Container Garden,” which has only seven archived performances, and “Slow West Vultures,” a bustout first heard in 53 archived shows [1]. The song “Earth Air Water Trees” is a legendary rarity, as this is the only archived performance of it [1]. Other rare tracks include “Surrounded,” “Cleaning Crew,” and “Only One Way” [1]. The set concludes with “No Children” [1]. Listeners who reviewed this specific recording praised it highly, with one noting it was a lovely tape and expressing curiosity about the sound of the Oktavas [2]. Another reviewer described it as a phenomenal pull of a great show, specifically highlighting that the song “Waylon Jennings Live!” slaps [3]. The recording has a perfect 5/5 rating from two listeners [1].",
